  << /ActualText (Conducted a literature review of RFC errata and revision practices\054 identifying bottlenecks in\ncurrent manual correction practices and motivating LLM automation beyond error detection\nProposed an automated correction methodology based on the group\220s prior work\054 extending LLMs from detection\055only to detection and repair\nCurated and cleaned 270 errata records across 80 RFCs with rigorous quality control\054 producing a high\055quality dataset for LLM training and evaluation\nCurrently fine\055tuning domain\055specific LLMs and building protocol\055aware NLP evaluation pipelines)
